--- !u!114 &-932023539296956625
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "The <b>Player Menu</b> can be accessed using either hands or controllers.\n\nWhen using hands, simply rotate your wrist so that your palm is facing up, a <b>Menu</b> button will be displayed on your wrist.\n\nWhen using controllers, rotate either controller to display the poke button or press the physical <b>Menu</b> button on the left controller.\n\nThe <b>Player Menu</b> features a side panel with the following options:\n   \xB7<b>Current Room Info</b>- Displays the current Room Code, Room Name, Room Privacy status (public/ private) and a list of all <b>Participants</b> (connected players).\n<b>Note:</b><i>Only the Host player can edit the room name and privacy.</i>\n\n   \xB7<b>Appearance Options</b>- Displays a Player Avatar mirror image, an input field UI element to edit the <b>Player Name</b> and a button to randomly change the assigned <b>Player Icon Color.</b>\n<b>Note:</b>only the Host Player Avatar will display a crown.\n\n   \xB7<b>Public Rooms List</b>- Displays options to <b>Leave</b> the current room, <b>Join</b> or <b>Create</b> a new room.\n\n   \xB7<b>Player Settings</b>-Displays a collapsable list of editable Audio and Locomotion options. \n\n   \xB7<b>Microphone Toggle</b>-Switches the microphone from active to inactive. "
