--- !u!114 &8224799270626597278
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'The <b>Music Player UI</b> prefab is a fully working networked UI example that shows how to synchronize UI elements across the network. This prefab has some options like <b>Auto Start</b> as well as the ability to assign any audio clips to be chosen from the dropdown menu.


      Interacting with any of the buttons will reflect those changes over the network. This prefab will also synchronize it''s state with new players when they join the room.


      Dig in to learn more about <b>Networked Buttons, Networked Toggles, Networked Sliders</b> and <b>Networked Dropdowns.</b>'
